      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "DateTime::Lite versions before 0.8.1 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via a per-day loop when adding seconds.\n\n_normalize_leap_seconds crosses day boundaries one day at a time, so add(seconds => $n) on an object with a non-floating time zone takes about |$n|/86400 iterations, and nothing limits $n. The XS implementation and the pure-Perl fallback both have the loop.\n\nAn attacker who controls the number of seconds added can keep the process busy for as long as they choose.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
